Robot models and data vendored in this repository

- MuJoCo Menagerie (Google DeepMind), https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie
  — the ALOHA 2 model under robots/aloha2-nominal/ (BSD-3-Clause, upstream
  commit da76818e) and the SO-101 / SO-ARM100 model under
  robots/so101-nominal/ (Apache-2.0). The upstream files are byte-identical;
  our wrappers (aloha2.xml, so101.xml) add sensors only.
- microduck_rl (Pollen Robotics), https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl
  — the walking robot's model and its 38 meshes under robots/microduck/
  (Apache-2.0, upstream commit d424a0c8).
- Robotiq 2F-85 gripper (Robotiq Inc.), https://github.com/robotiq/isaacsim_assets
  — the USD asset Robotiq_2F_85.usda (commit 6d992b6) imported as the
  bundle robots/robotiq-2f85-isaac/ (CC-BY-4.0; attribution required and
  given here and in the bundle's README). trainnr is not affiliated with
  Robotiq.
- BAM: Better Actuator Models (Rhoban), https://github.com/Rhoban/bam
  — the identified friction parameters of eight actuators under
  robots/actuators/ and the derived bundles under robots/actuator-bundles/
  (Apache-2.0; each actuator's PROVENANCE.json names the source and the
  citation, ICRA 2025).
- unitree_rl_mjlab (Unitree Robotics), https://github.com/unitreerobotics/unitree_rl_mjlab
  — the Unitree Go2 walk task's declared constants (gains, limits, home
  pose, joint order) read from src/assets/robots/unitree_go2/ (commit
  1425b15) into trainnr-mjlab/src/trainnr_mjlab/go2_walk.py (Apache-2.0).
  The Go2 model itself is not distributed here; onboarding reads it from
  the user's checkout.

Public telemetry the tools can fetch (not distributed here; licence state
is recorded on every recording the tools make from them)

- leg-odometry (Yibin Wu et al.), https://github.com/YibinWu/leg-odometry
  — a real Go2's /lowstate bag (repository MIT, the bag unlabelled).
- DFKI Robotics Innovation Center, Zenodo record 19336009 — a real Go2 on
  Vulcano Island, field201 (CC-BY-4.0).
- sim2real-robot-identification (IIT DLSLab),
  https://github.com/iit-DLSLab/sim2real-robot-identification — the Go2
  chirp traj_0.pt (BSD-3-Clause).

Scenes used in the recorded experiments (not distributed here)

- Mip-NeRF 360 (Barron et al., Google Research) — the "garden" capture,
  reconstructed and walked as a scene in docs/findings/ under the dataset's
  own terms.
- Neverwhere (Ran et al.) — the Go1 parkour scenes imported by
  trainnr/trainnr/scenes/neverwhere.py (MIT).

Software this product depends on (no source copied)

- MuJoCo (Google DeepMind, Apache-2.0) — the simulator.
- mjlab (mujocolab, Apache-2.0) — the reinforcement-learning trainer
  trainnr-mjlab plugs into.
- Rerun (Rerun Technologies, MIT or Apache-2.0) — the viewer embedded in
  the Studio through the re_viewer and re_ui crates, and the SDK the
  streams are written with.
- Newton (NVIDIA and the newton-physics project, Apache-2.0) — the USD
  importer behind the USD onboarding path.
- LeRobot (Hugging Face, Apache-2.0) — training, datasets, policy loading
  and the evaluator's environment contract; trainnr/trainnr/envs/lerobot_plugin.py
  implements its EnvConfig interface.
- gym-aloha / ACT (Tony Z. Zhao et al.; Hugging Face, Apache-2.0 / MIT) —
  the transfer-cube task under trainnr/trainnr/tasks/aloha2/ follows the
  original simulator's spawn box, cube contact parameters and top-camera
  placement so released checkpoints see the scene they were trained on.
- Gymnasium (Farama Foundation, MIT).

- docs/paper/latex/neurips_2023.sty: the NeurIPS 2023 LaTeX style file,
  fetched 2026-09-08 from media.neurips.cc and redistributed unmodified
  for the paper's layout. The file states no licence of its own; it is the
  conference's public style file, used as the conference publishes it.
